\newlabel{fig:promptset-vs-fixed}{{4}{10}{Fixed-prompt versus prompt-set evaluation across fine-tuning. Left: the single fixed $O$-prompt readout that produced the spurious ``collapse.'' Right: the 64-prompt sampled evaluation --- broad misalignment rises and \emph {stays}; what grows late is the domain-flip. The single-prompt collapse was an artifact of evaluating one point in prompt space.\relax }{figure.caption.6}{}}
